# Keep these out of the agent's reach.
#
# Important: .cursorignore is NOT a security boundary. Cursor's own documentation states that
# terminal and MCP tools can still reach ignored files. This is a second layer, not the first one.
# The first layer is: secrets never enter this repository at all.
#
# No negation (!) patterns are used here — a known Cursor regression prevents ! from overriding
# .gitignore exclusions while Instant Grep is enabled.

# Secrets — never
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.jks
id_rsa
id_ed25519
credentials.json
secrets.json
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
**/local.properties

# Cursor's own audit trail — noise in context, useful only when read deliberately
.cursor/audit.log
.cursor/mcp.json

# Build output and dependencies
node_modules/
dist/
build/
out/
.next/
coverage/
.gradle/
*.apk
*.aab
*.iml

# Editor and OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
